course: dictionary
lesson: 14871
title: Realign: putting things back in line
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Realign is made of two parts. Align means to line things up in a straight row or the right position, and re- at the start often means again or back. So realign means to line things up again. «The mechanic had to realign the wheels of the car.» The wheels had moved out of line, and the mechanic put them back in the correct position.
explain: Realign also describes changing your plans, ideas or friendships to fit a new situation. «The school realigned its plans after the new rules came in.» Nothing was moved in a straight line here. The school changed what it wanted to do so that it fitted the new rules.
explain: Look at the words around realign to choose the right meaning. Wheels, teeth and pictures are physical things, so they mean put back in position. Countries, groups, plans and priorities are about changing direction, so they mean change to fit something new. «Her braces will slowly realign her crooked teeth.»
fact: Realign means to put things back into a straight line or the correct position.
fact: Realign also means to change your plans, ideas or friendships to fit a new situation.
fact: The forms of realign are realign, realigns, realigned and realigning.
fact: Useful phrases are «realign the wheels», «realign with» and «realign priorities».
fact: The re- at the start of realign often means again or back, which is a helpful clue.
exercise: «The mechanic had to realign the wheels of the car.» What does realign mean here? | Take the wheels off for ever | Paint a new colour | Wash them with soap and water | *Put back into a straight line
exercise: «The country realigned itself with its neighbours.» What does realigned suggest? | Went to sleep for a long time | *Changed its plans to fit a new situation | Built a tall wall around its land | Lost its map and got lost
exercise: Which word is another form of realign? | remove | *realigns | redo | rest
test: «Her braces will slowly realign her teeth.» What does realign mean here? | Count the teeth one by one | Paint the teeth white | *Move the teeth back into the right position | Pull the teeth out
test: «The school realigned its priorities after the flood.» What does realigned mean here? | *Changed what mattered most to fit the new situation | Shut the school for ever | Had a party for everyone | Lost all its books
exam: «The bus driver had to realign the mirror before the trip.» What does realign mean? | Break into small pieces | *Put back into the correct position | Clean with a soft cloth | Forget about it completely
